# Base URL of the API (Tomcat Application context must be /CoHabitAPI)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/CoHabitAPI/api/events

# Same test data as task.http (task-test-data.sql): only the emails are needed here, no ids
# tasktestroomshare       : owner, accepted1, accepted2, pending
# tasktestroomshare_other : owner_other, roomie_other
# The owner AND the accepted roomies can read and add events (the JSON field is called roomieEmail for both)
# A GET has no body: the email is sent in the URL (?email=...)
# Run the cases from top to bottom: cases 2 to 9 create the events that cases 10 to 18 read
# To start again from zero (in Oracle): DELETE FROM Event;  then COMMIT;
@owner = task_owner@test.be
@roomie1 = task_roomie_accepted1@test.be
@roomie2 = task_roomie_accepted2@test.be
@pending = task_roomie_pending@test.be
@noRoomshare = task_roomie_none@test.be
@otherRoomie = task_roomie_other@test.be

### 1. Types for the buttons of the pop up → 200, 5 types in this order: social, meeting, visit, task, other (each with "code" and "label")
GET {{baseUrl}}/types
Accept: application/json

### 2. A roomie adds a complete event → 201, {"event": {...}} with an id, "date": "2026-11-14", "startTime": "19:00", "endTime": "22:00", "type": "social"
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Soirée pizza",
  "description": "Chacun apporte une pizza",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "startTime": "19:00",
  "endTime": "22:00",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 3. The owner adds an event → 201 (the owner is a member of the roomshare too)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Réunion de la coloc",
  "description": "Budget et règles de vie",
  "date": "2026-11-20",
  "startTime": "18:30",
  "endTime": "19:30",
  "type": "meeting",
  "roomieEmail": "{{owner}}"
}

### 4. Only the required fields (title, date, type) → 201, "description": null, "startTime": null, "endTime": null
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Visite du plombier",
  "date": "2026-11-17",
  "type": "visit",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie2}}"
}

### 5. Spaces around the texts, a time with seconds, a type in capital letters → 201, title and description trimmed, "startTime": "10:00" (seconds cut), "type": "task"
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   Ménage de printemps   ",
  "description": "   Tout le monde participe   ",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "startTime": "10:00:45",
  "endTime": "12:00",
  "type": "  TASK ",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 6. What the front sends when the user chose no time and no description (empty texts) → 201, "description": null, "startTime": null, "endTime": null
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Fête d'anniversaire",
  "description": "",
  "date": "2026-11-25",
  "startTime": "",
  "endTime": "",
  "type": "other",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 7. Last day of the month → 201 (it must be in the November list of case 10)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Paiement du loyer",
  "date": "2026-11-30",
  "type": "task",
  "roomieEmail": "{{owner}}"
}

### 8. First day of the next month → 201 (it must NOT be in the November list of case 10)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Marché de Noël",
  "date": "2026-12-01",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie2}}"
}

### 9. Last day of the previous month → 201 (it must NOT be in the November list of case 10)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Soirée Halloween",
  "date": "2026-10-31",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie2}}"
}

### 10. List of the month (what the calendar sends) → 200, 6 events
# In this order (sorted by date, then by id): Soirée pizza and Ménage de printemps (14/11), Visite du plombier (17/11),
# Réunion de la coloc (20/11), Fête d'anniversaire (25/11), Paiement du loyer (30/11)
# NOT in the list: Soirée Halloween (31/10) and Marché de Noël (01/12)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 11. List from a date, no end (what the home card sends) → 200, 7 events: the 6 of case 10 + Marché de Noël (not Halloween, it is before the 10th)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-10
Accept: application/json

### 12. The other accepted roomie of the same roomshare → 200, exactly the same answer as case 10 (the calendar is shared)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie2}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 13. The owner → 200, exactly the same answer as case 10 (the owner and the roomies find their roomshare in two different ways)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{owner}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 14. A roomie of the other roomshare → 200, [] (he does not see the events of tasktestroomshare)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{otherRoomie}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 15. The two limits are included: from = to = 2026-11-14 → 200, 2 events (Soirée pizza, then Ménage de printemps)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-14&to=2026-11-14
Accept: application/json

### 16. A period without event → 200, []
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2027-01-01&to=2027-01-31
Accept: application/json

### 17. Email with spaces and uppercase → 200, same answer as case 10 (cleaned like the login)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email=%20%20TASK_ROOMIE_ACCEPTED1@test.be%20&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 18. Empty "to" → 200, same answer as case 11 (an empty end date means no end)
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-10&to=
Accept: application/json

### 19. Missing "from" → 400, "The start date is required."
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 20. "from" with a wrong format → 400, "The start date must have the format YYYY-MM-DD."
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=14-11-2026
Accept: application/json

### 21. "to" with a wrong format → 400, "The end date must have the format YYYY-MM-DD."
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-01&to=demain
Accept: application/json

### 22. "to" before "from" → 400, "The end date cannot be before the start date."
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-30&to=2026-11-01
Accept: application/json

### 23. Missing email → 400, "Email is required"
GET {{baseUrl}}?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 24. Unknown email → 401, "The received user does not exist"
GET {{baseUrl}}?email=nobody@mail.be&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 25. A pending roomie → 403, "You must be an accepted member of a roomshare."
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{pending}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 26. A roomie without roomshare → 403, "You must be an accepted member of a roomshare."
GET {{baseUrl}}?email={{noRoomshare}}&from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
Accept: application/json

### 27. Missing title → 400, "The event title is required."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 28. Title longer than 100 characters (here 121) → 400, "The event title cannot be longer than 100 characters."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789X",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 29. Description longer than 255 characters (here 300) → 400, "The event description cannot be longer than 255 characters."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Description trop longue",
  "description": "",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 30. Missing date → 400, "The event date is required."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Sans date",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 31. Wrong date format → 400, "The event date must have the format YYYY-MM-DD."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mauvaise date",
  "date": "14/11/2026",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 32. A date that does not exist → 400, "The event date must have the format YYYY-MM-DD."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Le 30 février",
  "date": "2026-02-30",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 33. Wrong time format → 400, "The time must have the format HH:MM."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mauvaise heure",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "startTime": "7pm",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 34. End before the start → 400, "The end must be after the start."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Fin avant le début",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "startTime": "20:00",
  "endTime": "19:00",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 35. End equal to the start → 400, "The end must be after the start."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Fin égale au début",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "startTime": "20:00",
  "endTime": "20:00",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 36. Missing type → 400, "The event type is required."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Sans type",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 37. Unknown type → 400, "Invalid event type."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Type bizarre",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "party",
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 38. Missing email → 400, "Email is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Sans email",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social"
}

### 39. Unknown email → 401, "The received user does not exist"
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Personne",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "nobody@mail.be"
}

### 40. A pending roomie adds an event → 403, "You must be an accepted member of a roomshare."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Event du roomie en attente",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{pending}}"
}

### 41. A roomie without roomshare adds an event → 403, "You must be an accepted member of a roomshare."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Event du roomie sans coloc",
  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "type": "social",
  "roomieEmail": "{{noRoomshare}}"
}

### 42. Broken JSON → 400, "JSON invalid."
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Cassé",

### 43. Unknown extra field → 201 (ignored: the event is created in the roomshare of the caller, not in 999)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Champ en trop",
  "date": "2027-03-01",
  "type": "other",
  "roomshareId": 999,
  "roomieEmail": "{{roomie1}}"
}

### 44. Wrong Content-Type → 415
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: text/plain

hello

### 45. Wrong HTTP method → 405 (there is no PUT on /api/events)
PUT {{baseUrl}}?email={{roomie1}}&from=2026-11-01
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### CORS preflight (what the browser sends) → 200, the answer has the header Access-Control-Allow-Origin: http://127.0.0.1:5501
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:5501
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type